lined block, not a single config.effective_* call.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f187e23d7c7642e8e","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section: Approach ('each _effective_*_for helper routes its config.effective_* call through it')","norm_id":"n471348bc5613b5a9","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Use a single consistent kwarg name for the threaded memo dict across outbound_differ.py and outbound_mutation_builders.py (or note explicitly why the names differ).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.686,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope: 'add an optional `cache` kwarg to the six `_effective_*_for` helpers'","Scope: 'add an `effective_cache` kwarg to `_compute_outbound_create_mutation` / `_compute_outbound_update_mutation`'"],"finding":"The threaded memo object is named 'cache' in outbound_differ.py helpers but 'effective_cache' in outbound_mutation_builders.py, introducing minor terminology drift for the same object.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe979cbfacd00cccc","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section (outbound_differ.py and outbound_mutation_builders.py bullets)","norm_id":"n0c5064902e5c9119","priority":0.264,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader tracing the memo dict across the two modules must map 'effective_cache' to 'cache' for the same value."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Name the kwarg 'effective_cache' consistently in both modules (or 'cache' in both).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Record the redundancy magnitude motivating the memo (typical/observed N tickets, M distinct projects, and resulting `effective_*` call count per pass) in Context/Problem so the perf-only optimization is grounded in evidence rather than assumed scale.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'This is perf-only: the result is identical for a given (project_key, root) within a pass'","Plan Testing: 'Perf oracle (call-count proxy, not wall-clock)'","Verified redundancy exists (each `_effective_*_for` re-invokes `config.effective_*` → `load_mapping_config` → `read_reserved_section` per ticket per axis), but no magnitude for N or M is stated anywhere in the plan","G-9: raise a scale/optimization finding only when profiling/estimate/AC evidence exists; here the plan supplies none, so this is coaching to record that evidence rather than a block"],"finding":"The change is described as 'perf-only' and threads a new `cache`/`effective_cache` kwarg through 8 functions across 2 modules, but the plan cites no profiling result, scale estimate, or AC quantifying N (ticket count) or the per-call filesystem-walk cost — so there is no evidence the redundant discovery is a measured problem rather than a micro-optimization. The test's own oracle is an explicit call-count proxy 'not wall-clock', confirming no observed perf issue backs the work.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f15a3a6f9fa8e091c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem + Testing (perf oracle: 'call-count proxy, not wall-clock')","norm_id":"nb9474ee8f8191e73","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer/maintainer later asks whether threading a cache kwarg through 6 helpers + 2 builders was justified for the observed N (e.g. small stores where M≈N or N is tiny)"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Add a sentence to Approach justifying the differ-local per-axis memo over a config/mapping_config-layer memo of load_mapping_config(root) (which would reduce the walk to once per pass) — e.g. cite smaller blast-radius / avoiding core-config state.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Verified src/.../config.py:effective_status_map and mapping_config.py:load_mapping_config: load_mapping_config has NO caching and re-reads read_reserved_section every call; each of the 6 helpers calls it once per (axis, project) => 6*M walks under the plan's memo.","A config-layer memo keyed on root alone would yield 1 walk/pass and also benefit _assert_type_decisions_for_pass and other config.effective_* callers.","Plan's stated goal 'once per distinct project per axis' is met by the chosen approach, so it is defensible — this is a missed-better-alternative coaching note, not a blocker."],"finding":"The plan's memo reduces the stat-walk from ~N-per-axis to M-per-axis (6*M total load_mapping_config calls), but a structurally-different alternative — memoizing at the config/mapping_config I/O seam (cache load_mapping_config(root) once per pass) — collapses all six axes and all projects to a single walk per pass and is simpler (one memo point at the true source of the walk). The plan should acknowledge and justify why the differ-local per-axis memo is preferred (e.g. smaller blast-radius / no core-config state) over the layer-level memo.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2a7a548b4c8aae38","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section: Approach","norm_id":"n9edfc68d19281746","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Realign leaf-to-parent containment: either narrow the leaf to the STATUS axis that parent 438a actually scopes (the advisory's subject) — deferring type/priority/create-defaults/link/excluded-sync-types caching and the `outbound_mutation_builders.py` edit — OR re-parent this cross-axis perf change under a parent whose plan contains all six `_effective_*_for` axes (updating that parent first so its plan-review re-runs).","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.85,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent 438a title/Approach: 'Config-driven status mapp